questions.prompt:
Find the bug and fix it:

```js
async function placeOrder(order) {
  await db.query('INSERT INTO orders (id, total) VALUES ($1, $2)', [order.id, order.total]);
  await kafka.send('order-created', { id: order.id, total: order.total });
}
```

What can go wrong, and how does the **transactional outbox** pattern fix it? What must consumers of the event still do?

questions.answer:
```js
async function placeOrder(order) {
  await db.transaction(async (tx) => {
    await tx.query('INSERT INTO orders (id, total) VALUES ($1, $2)', [order.id, order.total]);
    await tx.query('INSERT INTO outbox (id, topic, payload) VALUES ($1, $2, $3)',
      [crypto.randomUUID(), 'order-created', JSON.stringify({ id: order.id, total: order.total })]);
  });
}
// relay: SELECT unsent outbox rows → kafka.send → mark sent (at-least-once)
```
